00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:21,520
C, opossum. D, your sister?

254
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:24,520
Oh, I'm so confused.

255
00:12:34,220 --> 00:12:37,040
Sure, they're happy now, but cheaters never win.

256
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:39,520
Eventually, they're gonna get...

257
00:12:40,620 --> 00:12:50,540
an A. Mom, Dad, I think the first thing that my report card will show you is that I

258
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:55,040
didn't cheat. I can do better than that.

259
00:12:56,180 --> 00:12:59,060
You know, I don't think my report card is that important in light of the recent

260
00:12:59,060 --> 00:13:00,300
events in the Soviet Union.

261
00:13:02,220 --> 00:13:05,140
Now, if I mention the Soviet Union, they're gonna bring up my grade and current

262
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:12,240
events. Okay. Now, the best thing to do is just not to mention my report card at

263
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:14,900
all. Just keep it under my hat until I see which way the wind blows.

264
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:17,680
Yeah, I think I can do that.

265
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:23,000
Yo, Benny. Hey, Mike, what are you doing here?

266
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:24,320
Having lunch with my friends.

267
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,360
Are Mom and Dad around?

268
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:30,860
Ah, report card day.

269
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,140
How do you know?

270
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:34,280
Benny, I can smell the fear in the air.

271
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:35,460
Smells like defeat.

272
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:37,440
Mike, what are you doing here?

273
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:39,860
You moved out and you spend more time here than I do.

274
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:40,640
Get a life.

275
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:42,460
Benny, Benny, come on, relax.

276
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:44,020
I've been through this a lot more than you have.

277
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:44,960
Here, maybe I can help.

278
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:45,860
Nobody can help.

279
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:47,800
Look, it's never as bad as it seems.

280
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:50,700
You got enough money for a bus ticket out of town?

281
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:52,720
It's not that bad.

282
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:53,900
I got an A in health.

283
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:55,440
Ooh, Benny, that's bad.

284
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:59,020
Why? Because it shows them that you can do it if you want to.

285
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:01,340
And it makes every other grade look like a bitter failure.

286
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:03,340
Failures? What failures?

287
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:04,580
My lowest grade's a D.

288
00:14:05,060 --> 00:14:06,580
Ooh, D is worse than an F.

289
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:07,800
How do you figure?

290
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:10,520
Well, all right, you got an F.

291
00:14:11,340 --> 00:14:13,060
One line on the side makes it an A.

292
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:15,880
What the heck of a lot you can do with a D.

293
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:22,320
Hi, guys. Mmm, smells like report card day.

294
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:24,800
So, is it you, Mike, or Ben?

295
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:26,660
Oh, or is it both of you?

296
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:27,920
Calm down, Carol.

297
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:28,720
It's just me.

298
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:33,380
Oh, well, as long as you do the best you could, Mom and Dad won't get too upset.

299
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:36,980
Carol, go pump your sunshine someplace else, okay?

300
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,560
I mean, that boy is twisting in the wind here.

301
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:41,940
So, how's everybody this fine?

302
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:46,280
And... report card day.

303
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:48,440
I'll get Mom.

304
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:49,580
Thank you, Carol.

305
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:51,700
Listen, Ben, I gotta run.

306
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:55,740
You're leaving? Yeah, well, I don't want any of what's coming your way to land on

307
00:14:55,740 --> 00:15:02,340
me. Ben, we don't get upset as long as you do your best, but a D is not your best,

308
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:03,160
and you know it.

309
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:05,680
You're starting high school next year, and it's only gonna get tougher.

310
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:10,060
I hope this two -week grounding is gonna impress upon you the fact you cannot let a

311
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:12,880
class slide all semester and then suddenly catch up in one night.

312
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:15,720
That means no TV, no hanging out after school with your friends.

313
00:15:15,780 --> 00:15:17,320
You are up in your room studying.

314
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:20,060
Perhaps you overlooked my A in health.

315
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:23,220
That only proves that you can do it if you want to.

316
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:28,260
And if you can't pull up that D on your final report card, you're gonna be doing

317
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:29,300
time in summer school.

318
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:32,580
Um, you know, I could have gotten an A.

319
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:34,060
By cheating, Ben?

320
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:35,500
