333
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:14,100
Mike. Zach. Of course, he turned out all right.

334
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:15,600
No, he didn't.

335
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:18,840
Hi, guys. Look, I'm Pete.

336
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,540
We just wanted to tell you more good news.

337
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:23,680
When our parents saw our report cards, they gave us money.

338
00:16:24,540 --> 00:16:25,300
Come on, Ben.

339
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:26,900
Let me buy you a freezy -weezy.

340
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:30,120
Oh, look, I'm not going anywhere for two weeks.

341
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:33,160
I'm grounded. Well, you got nobody to blame but yourself.

342
00:16:33,180 --> 00:16:34,940
You could ace that test like we did.

343
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:36,180
Ha, I know, Vito.

344
00:16:36,180 --> 00:16:38,020
I know. So why the heck didn't you?

345
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:41,780
Because I was stupid enough to believe my father when he told me cheaters never win.

346
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:43,620
Oh, Ben, Ben, Ben, where you been?

347
00:16:43,980 --> 00:16:45,140
Parents lie all the time.

348
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:47,620
My folks told me all kinds of crazy stuff that ain't true.

349
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:51,960
Mine too. Every night when my mom goes to tuck me in, she tells me I'm tall.

350
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:54,720
Look, I gotta go.

351
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:55,860
Look on the bright side.

352
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:58,520
At least you learned that when you want the truth, you come to your friends.

353
00:16:58,720 --> 00:16:59,600
Not your old man.

354
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:00,920
You said it.

355
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:15,540
Well, I'm glad I'm not being graded on my performance the last 24 hours.

356
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:17,840
Oh, Jason, you were wonderful.

357
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:20,420
I'm not talking about last night.

358
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,060
Neither was I.

359
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:39,780
Got a minute?

360
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:42,480
A minute? I believe I got two weeks.

361
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:45,260
Well, I've got to apologize.

362
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:47,200
I've, uh, made a terrible mistake.

363
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:49,060
So you mean I'm not grounded?

364
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:50,360
Oh, Dad, I forgive you.

365
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:52,000
See ya. No, no, hey, wait, wait, Ben.

366
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:53,980
Grounding was the only thing I did right.

367
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,960
Oh, so it's gonna be one of those talks?

368
00:17:57,820 --> 00:17:59,420
Those talks? Nothing.

369
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:05,840
Go on. Well, the, uh, advice I gave you last week about cheating, Ben, was, uh, was

370
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:07,400
wrong. Sure was.

371
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,060
I'm not saying it was wrong.

372
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:10,920
I mean, uh, it was incomplete.

373
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:13,240
Oh, so it is gonna be one of those talks.

374
00:18:13,860 --> 00:18:15,400
Ben, don't pout like a kid.

375
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:16,960
Come on, I'm trying to talk to you as an adult.

376
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:20,920
Look, when I told you that cheaters never win, Ben, I thought that was all you

377
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:21,380
needed to know.

378
00:18:21,380 --> 00:18:22,780
But there is a lot more to it.

379
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:25,700
Because, uh, cheaters do win.

380
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:28,080
Not only do they win, they win cash.

381
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:30,580
Sometimes it's even bigger than that.

382
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:32,820
Sometimes they win gold medals at the Olympics.

383
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:35,560
On a rare occasion, they even win the White House.

384
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,160
Dad, I'm not following this.

385
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:44,300
I mean, if you can cheat and get away with it, then what's wrong with it?

386
00:18:44,940 --> 00:18:48,680
Ben, the way you see cheating really depends on how you understand the whole world.

387
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:50,540
I don't understand it at all.

388
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:51,980
I got a D in science, remember?

389
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,200
Look, uh, why are we on this earth, Ben?

390
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:58,540
What's the point of our lives?

391
00:18:59,020 --> 00:19:00,460
You know, I mean, we all have to make a choice.

392
00:19:00,600 --> 00:19:02,900
You either see things as order or chaos.

393
00:19:03,420 --> 00:19:06,920
And if you see the world as chaos, then, uh, then there's no point in life at all.

394
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,160
You know, nothing matters.

395
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:09,700
And we're all just a bunch of people running around.

396
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:13,120
We're bumping into each other, having fun, making noises till we die.

397
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:16,540
We're just taking up space, Ben, and I can't believe in that.

398
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:23,940
But look, if you see the world as having order, Ben, then there's a reason to

399
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:25,800
everything. There's a reason to get up in the morning.

400
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,960
There's a reason to make something of your life.

401
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:30,200
There's a reason for learning, Ben.

402
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:31,300
It all fits together.

403
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:35,160
And if learning is important, then cheating is wrong.

404
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:36,880
Even when you get away with it?

405
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:38,080
What's getting away with it?

406
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,040
Not getting caught.

407
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:40,520
Which means? Getting an A.

408
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:41,600
So what does the A mean?

409
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,860
Ten bucks. What does it mean you've learned?

410
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,220
Nothing. Well then you've been cheating for nothing.

411
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:47,380
Yes. What's the point in it?

412
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:48,300
Does there have to be a point?

413
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:49,680
Yes, better there's care.

414
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:56,760
So you're saying there should be a point in what I'm doing all the time?

415
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:01,200
Yes. I don't think I like being talked to as an adult.

416
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:04,840
Well, sometimes none of us do.

417
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:09,860
Dad, has anybody really given this chaos thing a fair chance?

418
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:13,840
Mike came close.

419
00:20:17,940 --> 00:20:19,480
Are you getting any of this?

420
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:24,680
Yeah, well, I'm starting to realize that cheaters really don't win, but I couldn't

421
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:28,240
explain it. Well, then you're exactly where I was two weeks ago when I couldn't

422
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:29,080
explain it to you.

423
00:20:29,620 --> 00:20:30,500
Wait a minute.

424
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:35,440
If the point of school is really learning stuff, then I gotta do homework every

425
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:39,060
night, and I gotta study all the time, and I gotta meet you.

426
00:20:39,060 --> 00:20:39,540
Wait, wait, wait.

427
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:40,840
Hold on. One step at a time, Ben.

428
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:42,340
I don't want you exploding on me.

429
00:20:46,060 --> 00:20:50,860
Look, uh, what I want you to realize, Ben, is that it's time for you to make a

430
00:20:50,860 --> 00:20:53,720
choice. Order or chaos.

431
00:20:56,160 --> 00:21:00,620
Well, I think, uh, we've just had our first adult conversation.

432
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:04,780
Yeah. We did, didn't we?

433
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:10,080
You promised we don't have to have another one for a real long time.

434
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:18,240
Deal. Dad, is there any chance that our adult conversation means I'm not grounded

435
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:21,420
anymore? No chance at all.

436
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:30,640
Just checking. If there's a point to everything, maybe that blonde in the leotard

437
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:31,320
will be back.

438
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:36,020
I can teach her something about order, like following him.

439
00:21:37,660 --> 00:21:41,500
No, Ben. It's worth a shot.

440
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:54,380
We'll be back in a moment.

441
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:22,840
I'm gonna be a good boy.

442
00:22:22,840 --> 00:22:29,040
I'm gonna be a good boy.

443
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:31,720
I'm gonna be a good boy.

444
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,360
I'm gonna be a good boy.

445
00:22:34,360 --> 00:22:34,440
I'm gonna be a good boy.

446
00:22:34,460 --> 00:22:35,120
I'm gonna be a good boy.

447
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:36,220
I'm gonna be a good boy.

448
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:36,700
I'm gonna be a good boy.

449
00:22:36,700 --> 00:22:37,840
I'm gonna be a good boy.
